MedlinePlus Genetics summaries (public domain)
----------------------------------------------
The public HG002 demo release carries gene and condition summaries from MedlinePlus Genetics
(https://medlineplus.gov/genetics/), the explanations' grounding. They are the National Library
of Medicine's own text, in the public domain; the Library asks that it be credited as the
source and implies no endorsement of this software. Unmodified; no file of the repository
carries them.


RBCeq2 allele positions (MIT)
-----------------------------
src/genokeeper/resources/bloodgroups/rbceq2_2.4.4_positions.tsv is cut from the GRCh38 column
of rbceq2/resources/db.tsv inside the rbceq2 2.4.4 wheel (https://github.com/limcintyre/RBCeq2),
Copyright 2025 Australian Red Cross Lifeblood, under the MIT License
(https://opensource.org/license/mit), whose full text is that wheel's
rbceq2-2.4.4.dist-info/licenses/LICENSE. Modified: systems and positions only, the platelet
antigens, RH and MNS left out (the file's header says how).


GenCC
-----
tests/fixtures/gencc_head.tsv is the first rows of the Gene Curation Coalition's submissions
export (https://thegencc.org), and tests/fixtures/check_responses/gencc.headers a response
recorded from its download endpoint. GenCC releases its data under CC0 1.0
(https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/).


PharmGKB / ClinPGx clinical annotations (CC BY-SA 4.0)
------------------------------------------------------
src/genokeeper/resources/hla/alleles.tsv lists HLA alleles with the drugs, levels and annotation
IDs of PharmGKB's clinical annotations as frozen on 2025-07-05 (clinical_annotations.tsv,
clinical_ann_alleles.tsv; https://www.clinpgx.org), released under the Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 License (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/).
Modified: one allele per row, levels 2A and 2B of category Toxicity, plus disease rows cited to
their publications in the file's header. This file, as adapted material, is under CC BY-SA 4.0,
not the Apache License; attribution: PharmGKB/ClinPGx (Whirl-Carrillo M et al., Clin Pharmacol
Ther 2021, doi:10.1002/cpt.2350).


Publications whose tables are cited in resource files
-----------------------------------------------------
- src/genokeeper/resources/hla/dq_tags.tsv: the six HLA-DQ tag SNPs of Monsuur AJ et al., PLoS ONE
  2008;3:e2270 (doi:10.1371/journal.pone.0002270), an open-access article under a Creative
  Commons Attribution licence; positions from dbSNP (public domain).
- src/genokeeper/resources/hla/hg002_truth.tsv: HG002's HLA types from Chin CS et al., Nat Commun
  2020;11:4794 (doi:10.1038/s41467-020-18564-9, CC BY 4.0), checked against Immuannot's typing of
  the HPRC HG002 assemblies (Zhou et al., Genome Res 2024, doi:10.1101/gr.278985.124).
- src/genokeeper/resources/genelists/: the ACMG SF v3.3 and carrier Tier 3 gene lists (Genet Med
  2025 and 2021, cited in each file), and ClinGen's gene-disease validity export (CC0 1.0) for
  Tier 4.
- src/genokeeper/resources/mechanism_not_assessed.tsv: one GeneReviews chapter per gene (University
  of Washington, Seattle), cited by authors, NBK accession and PMID and summarised, not quoted.


Public-domain sources
---------------------
The gene, exon and coding spans under src/genokeeper/resources/ (af_guard/, coverage/, deletions/,
paralogs/, bs1_gene_spans.tsv) are cut from NCBI's MANE release 1.5 and NCBI Gene, the variant
positions from ClinVar and dbSNP, and the masked intervals and the HG002 truths from GIAB
(NIST): works of the United States government, each file naming its source and checksum.


Recorded API responses in tests
-------------------------------
tests/fixtures/check_responses/ holds responses recorded from public endpoints, mostly version
metadata: ClinVar (public domain), CPIC (CC0 1.0), gnomAD (CC0 1.0), the GWAS Catalog and the
PGS Catalog (EMBL-EBI terms of use), IPD-IMGT/HLA (a version string), ClinGen and GenCC (above),
and GitHub's release metadata of ExpansionHunter, Yleaf, Haplogrep3, STRchive and PharmCAT.


Aldy results and PharmVar allele names
--------------------------------------
tests/fixtures/aldy_cyp2d6_na10860.aldy and tests/fixtures/hg002/hg002.aldy.CYP2A6.txt are
results of Aldy 4.8.3 (https://github.com/0xTCG/aldy; Hari A et al., Genome Research 2023) on
public samples (GeT-RM NA10860, GIAB HG002), published with this acknowledgement as Aldy's
licence asks; tests/fixtures/aldy_cyp2b6.aldy is hand-written in its output shape. Their star
alleles are PharmVar's (https://www.pharmvar.org; Gaedigk A et al., Clin Pharmacol Ther 2018).


AlphaMissense sample row (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)
------------------------------------------
tests/test_bootstrap.py carries the header and the first data row of AlphaMissense_hg38.tsv as
a format sample (Cheng J et al., Science 2023; https://storage.googleapis.com/dm_alphamissense/), licensed
CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/). The full file is
fetched by each user and never redistributed.


